    <div class="Section1">
        
        <!-- COVER PAGE -->
        <div>
            <h1>QUANTIRA CONTENT OS</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">A Full-Stack Enterprise Content Operations, Workflow Automation, & Client Portal Application</p>
            
            <div class="cover-meta">
                <table>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Document Version:</strong> 1.0.0 (Production Build)</td>
                        <td><strong>Prepared By:</strong> Engineering Team</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Client Name:</strong> Quantira Portfolio Project</td>
                        <td><strong>Release Date:</strong> July 31, 2026</td>
                    </tr>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="page-break"></div>

        <!-- PROBLEM STATEMENT -->
        <section>
            <h2>1. Problem Statement</h2>
            <p>Modern digital marketing agencies and creative studios suffer from high operational latency due to the lack of unified coordination. Deliverables pass through a loose web of emails, chat channels, shared documents, design boards, and individual platform dashboards. This creates:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Approval Bottlenecks:</strong> Delays in campaigns because design feedback and editorial approvals get buried in clients' crowded inboxes.</li>
                <li><strong>Version Control Failures:</strong> Creative assets are frequently posted using incorrect draft formats due to unsynchronized asset folders.</li>
                <li><strong>Opaque Reporting:</strong> Consolidating post analytics (reach, impressions, leads, revenue) is manually executed via spreadsheets, meaning clients only see ROI weeks after campaigns conclude.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Quantira Content OS solves this by unifying creative intake, kanban production, editorial approvals, and post-publish analytics telemetry into a single, cohesive, role-based platform.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- DETAILED FUNCTIONALITY DOCUMENT -->
        <section>
            <h2>2. Detailed Functionality Document</h2>
            <p>Quantira Content OS provides a comprehensive operational pipeline partitioned into two main experiences:</p>
            
            <h3>A. Sandboxed Client Portal</h3>
            <p>Clients are securely isolated to their own dashboard view containing the following core modules:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Performance Telemetry Dashboard:</strong> Visualizes client impressions, reach, link clicks, leads, and generated revenue. Next.js server-side helpers pull these statistics dynamically.</li>
                <li><strong>Editorial Content Calendar:</strong> Displays upcoming scheduled posts in a grid. Clicking on a post opens a detail card housing the copywriting captions, platform flags, and a direct URL to review the creative asset (Canva/Drive).</li>
                <li><strong>One-Click Approval Interface:</strong> Clients can review the post directly inside the calendar and click "Approve" (which transitions the post status to 'Approved' and sets approval date) or request modifications.</li>
                <li><strong>Intake Request Hub:</strong> Clients can submit requests for new creative briefs (defining platforms, type, objectives, brief text, due dates, and priorities) directly into the database.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>B. Creative Operations Console</h3>
            <p>Internal staff use this interface to track work and coordinate production:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Kanban Board Pipeline:</strong> Move content items dynamically through progress flags (Intake, Copywriting, Designing, Audit, Client Review, Published).</li>
                <li><strong>QA Scorecard Module:</strong> Quality reviewers grade posts across Reach Potential, Hook Style, Lead Quality, and Call-To-Action (CTA) strength. The system calculates a weighted overall quality score out of 10.</li>
                <li><strong>Campaign Configuration:</strong> Admin and Account Managers set up campaigns, allocate budgets, track expected revenues, and assign roles.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- USE CASES -->
        <section>
            <h2>3. Use Cases</h2>
            
            <h3>Use Case 1: Client Brief Intake</h3>
            <p><strong>Actor:</strong> Client Stakeholder</p>
            <p><strong>Goal:</strong> Submit a brief for an upcoming product launch campaign.</p>
            <p><strong>Flow:</strong> Client logs in -> Navigates to 'New Request' -> Fills platform target (e.g. LinkedIn), content objective, text description, due date, and priority -> Submits request. The request is logged in the DB as 'Open' and alert notification is generated for the Account Manager.</p>

            <h3>Use Case 2: Copy & Design Production</h3>
            <p><strong>Actor:</strong> Copywriter & Designer</p>
            <p><strong>Goal:</strong> Add creative assets to a content draft.</p>
            <p><strong>Flow:</strong> Copywriter claims the drafted item -> Fills caption text and hashtags -> Designer adds Canva graphics link -> Reviewer receives automated state change notification.</p>

            <h3>Use Case 3: Quality Review Scoring</h3>
            <p><strong>Actor:</strong> Reviewer</p>
            <p><strong>Goal:</strong> Verify content quality and brand safety prior to client exposure.</p>
            <p><strong>Flow:</strong> Reviewer accesses the post -> Fills in scores (1-10) for Reach, Hook, and CTA -> System calculates overall grade -> Post is approved for client review and displays on the calendar.</p>

            <h3>Use Case 4: Client Approval & Sign-Off</h3>
            <p><strong>Actor:</strong> Client Stakeholder</p>
            <p><strong>Goal:</strong> Sign off on a post scheduled for publication.</p>
            <p><strong>Flow:</strong> Client opens the interactive editorial calendar -> Clicks the post -> Reviews visual asset and copy -> Clicks 'Approve'. Post is flagged as 'Approved', and ready for publishing.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- KEY FEATURES -->
        <section>
            <h2>4. Key Features</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):</strong> Secure routing checks block clients from accessing agency financials, billing databases, and backend administrative panels.</li>
                <li><strong>Automated Database Seeding:</strong> Schema setup includes predefined seed models for admins, creative staff, default campaigns, and historical metrics.</li>
                <li><strong>Telemetry Ingestion:</strong> Dynamically calculates lead generation cost and campaign ROI in real time.</li>
                <li><strong>Edge Middleware Guarding:</strong> Performs session token lookup at the edge to optimize redirect latency.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- TECHNOLOGY STACK -->
        <section>
            <h2>5. Technology Stack Used</h2>
            <table class="data-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Layer</th>
                        <th>Technology</th>
                        <th>Purpose / Application</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Web Framework</strong></td>
                        <td>Next.js 14.2.1 (React 18)</td>
                        <td>Server-side rendering, App Router routing, and client views.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>UI Component System</strong></td>
                        <td>Ant Design (Antd)</td>
                        <td>Interactive grids, editorial calendars, forms, and tables.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Styling</strong></td>
                        <td>TailwindCSS & Vanilla CSS</td>
                        <td>Modern typography, responsive layout styling.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Database Engine</strong></td>
                        <td>SQLite</td>
                        <td>Self-contained, relational SQL database.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>ORM Layer</strong></td>
                        <td>Prisma ORM</td>
                        <td>Type-safe database schema creation and seed scripts.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Authentication</strong></td>
                        <td>NextAuth.js (v5 Beta)</td>
                        <td>Role-based JWT session token handling and cookie routing.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Analytics Subsystem</strong></td>
                        <td>Python Streamlit 1.58.0</td>
                        <td>Alternative admin interface for data charting.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Hosting</strong></td>
                        <td>Vercel</td>
                        <td>Cloud hosting.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </section>

        <div class="page-break"></div>

        <!-- API DOCUMENTATION -->
        <section>
            <h2>6. API Documentation</h2>
            <p>Quantira Content OS implements structured JSON REST endpoints. Key routes include:</p>
            
            <h3>A. Content Requests Endpoint (`/api/requests`)</h3>
            <p>Handles the client intake briefs. Approving a request automatically creates production and performance database entries.</p>
            <div class="code-block">
GET /api/requests
Response:
[
  {
    "requestId": 1,
    "requestedBy": "client@acmecorp.com",
    "client": "Acme Corp",
    "platform": "LinkedIn",
    "contentType": "Infographic",
    "priority": "High",
    "brief": "Q3 product update brief...",
    "status": "Open"
  }
]
            </div>
            <div class="code-block">
PUT /api/requests
Body:
{
  "requestId": "1",
  "status": "Approved"
}
Response: 200 OK (Triggers automatic creation of ContentMaster draft + Production record)
            </div>

            <h3>B. Approvals Endpoint (`/api/approvals`)</h3>
            <p>Tracks client signatures and comments.</p>
            <div class="code-block">
PUT /api/approvals
Body:
{
  "contentId": "CNT-001",
  "approvalStatus": "Approved"
}
Response:
{
  "contentId": "CNT-001",
  "approvalStatus": "Approved",
  "finalApprovalDate": "2026-07-31T12:00:00.000Z"
}
            </div>
        </section>

