        <!-- MY CONTRIBUTION TO THE PROJECT -->
        <section>
            <h2>9. Engineering Contributions (By Antigravity)</h2>
            <p>During the deployment and verification phases, I performed the following key engineering contributions:</p>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Dynamic Cookie Name & Security Fix (src/middleware.ts):</strong> Debugged the login session loop on HTTPS Vercel proxies where NextAuth was dropping non-secure cookies (`authjs.session-token`) while the edge router expected secure names (`__Secure-authjs.session-token`). Wrote a custom parser to dynamically check for both secure and insecure variants in incoming cookie requests.</li>
                <li><strong>Vercel Build Target Optimization:</strong> Designed `.vercelignore` rules to exclude Streamlit python scripts (`app.py`, SQL initialize files) that Vercel's zero-config CLI was incorrectly trying to compile as python serverless functions, resolving build failures.</li>
                <li><strong>Database Config & Vercel Project Linking:</strong> Created a clean project scope configuration on Vercel CLI, injecting production variables (`DATABASE_URL`, `AUTH_SECRET`, `NEXTAUTH_SECRET`, `AUTH_TRUST_HOST`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`) to ensure successful Next.js serverless route deployment and Prisma DB pushes/seeds.</li>
                <li><strong>Source Code Setup:</strong> Standardized and pushed local workspace revisions onto your new target GitHub repository `SSM-tracker`.</li>
            </ol>
        </section>

